{"id":"7f7f26a10a4215f1","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-theorem.md","title":"Theorem","display":"df-theorem — Theorem","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-theorem","aliases":["58-df-theorem","Theorem"],"display":"df-theorem — Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch17/58-df-logic.md]]","[[../batch04/58-df-proof.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-structure.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md]]","[[../batch03/58-df-assignment.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-theorem"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-theorem</span><span>Theorem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-theorem — Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"44e32f3fb4334e0c\" href=\"?note=44e32f3fb4334e0c\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-logic.md\">../batch17/58-df-logic.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"68fd6aebcf2cd4ac\" href=\"?note=68fd6aebcf2cd4ac\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-proof.md\">../batch04/58-df-proof.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d9b8711cda3f31ca\" href=\"?note=d9b8711cda3f31ca\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-structure.md\">../batch18/58-df-structure.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md\">../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"64f35ba2e87964e0\" href=\"?note=64f35ba2e87964e0\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-assignment.md\">../batch03/58-df-assignment.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> (first-order signature), <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_S(\\Sigma)\">\\(\\Gamma\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_S(\\Sigma)\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\phi\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_S(\\Sigma)\">\\(\\phi\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_S(\\Sigma)\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal P\">\\(\\mathcal P\\)</span> (formal proof system over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathcal M,\\Sigma,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\">\\(\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathcal M,\\Sigma,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\\)</span> (object-level satisfaction package, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md\">../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal M,s)\">\\(\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal M,s)\\)</span> (assignment predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"64f35ba2e87964e0\" href=\"?note=64f35ba2e87964e0\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-assignment.md\">../batch03/58-df-assignment.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Proof}_{\\mathcal P}(p,\\Gamma,\\phi)\">\\(\\operatorname{Proof}_{\\mathcal P}(p,\\Gamma,\\phi)\\)</span> (finite proof predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"68fd6aebcf2cd4ac\" href=\"?note=68fd6aebcf2cd4ac\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-proof.md\">../batch04/58-df-proof.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SemanticConsequence}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{SemanticConsequence}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TheoremOf}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{TheoremOf}_S\\)</span> (relations defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}theorem\\text{-}semantic} \\vdash \\operatorname{SemanticConsequence}_S(\\Sigma,\\Gamma,\\phi) \\leftrightarrow \\Gamma\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\\phi\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\\forall\\mathcal M,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat}\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathcal M,\\Sigma,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\\to\\bigl[(\\forall\\gamma\\in\\Gamma\\;\\forall s\\;(\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal M,s)\\to\\operatorname{Sat}(\\gamma,s)))\\to\\forall s\\;(\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal M,s)\\to\\operatorname{Sat}(\\phi,s))\\bigr]\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}theorem\\text{-}semantic} \\vdash \\operatorname{SemanticConsequence}_S(\\Sigma,\\Gamma,\\phi) \\leftrightarrow \\Gamma\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\\phi\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\\forall\\mathcal M,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat}\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathcal M,\\Sigma,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\\to\\bigl[(\\forall\\gamma\\in\\Gamma\\;\\forall s\\;(\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal M,s)\\to\\operatorname{Sat}(\\gamma,s)))\\to\\forall s\\;(\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal M,s)\\to\\operatorname{Sat}(\\phi,s))\\bigr]\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}theorem\\text{-}syntactic} \\vdash \\operatorname{TheoremOf}_S(\\mathcal P,\\Gamma,\\phi)\\leftrightarrow\\exists p\\;\\operatorname{Proof}_{\\mathcal P}(p,\\Gamma,\\phi)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}theorem\\text{-}syntactic} \\vdash \\operatorname{TheoremOf}_S(\\mathcal P,\\Gamma,\\phi)\\leftrightarrow\\exists p\\;\\operatorname{Proof}_{\\mathcal P}(p,\\Gamma,\\phi)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Theorem: formula derivable from axioms via rules of inference in formal system</li>\n<li>Semantic consequence is stated entirely through the registered satisfaction and assignment predicates, keeping the object language separate from the metalevel.</li>\n<li>Soundness is the metatheorem <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TheoremOf}_S(\\mathcal P,\\Gamma,\\phi)\\to\\operatorname{SemanticConsequence}_S(\\Sigma,\\Gamma,\\phi)\">\\(\\operatorname{TheoremOf}_S(\\mathcal P,\\Gamma,\\phi)\\to\\operatorname{SemanticConsequence}_S(\\Sigma,\\Gamma,\\phi)\\)</span> for a sound proof calculus <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal P\">\\(\\mathcal P\\)</span> over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span>; it is not a definition of a new predicate.</li>\n<li>Completeness (Gödel): <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma \\models \\phi \\implies \\Gamma \\vdash \\phi\">\\(\\Gamma \\models \\phi \\implies \\Gamma \\vdash \\phi\\)</span> for first-order logic</li>\n<li>Inconsistency: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma \\vdash \\bot\">\\(\\Gamma \\vdash \\bot\\)</span>; nontrivial theory proves neither all nor no formulas</li>\n<li>Independence: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma \\not\\vdash \\phi\">\\(\\Gamma \\not\\vdash \\phi\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma \\not\\vdash \\neg\\phi\">\\(\\Gamma \\not\\vdash \\neg\\phi\\)</span>: statement independent of axioms</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Enderton, A Mathematical Introduction to Logic</li>\n<li>Mendelson, Introduction to Mathematical Logic</li>\n<li>Shoenfield, Mathematical Logic</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch17/58-df-logic.md","status":"resolved","id":"44e32f